53073†doi.org L224: \nL225: Published in\nL226: \nL227: cite0†Frontiers in Molecular Biosciences L228: \nL229:   * #### cite63†Protein Folding, Misfolding and Degradation L230: \nL231:   * cite0†4.4 impact factor L232:   * cite0†8.9 citescore L233: \nL234: cite64†Part of a Research Topic Molecular Determinants of Protein Assemblies in Health and Disease, volume II 36k views 5 articles L235: ### Editor & Reviewers\nL236: \nL237: Edited by\nL238: \nL239: cite65†WA Walid A Houry University of Toronto, Canada†loop.frontiersin.org L240: \nL241: Reviewed by\nL242: \nL243: cite66†OG Olivier Genest CNRS UMR7281 Bioénergétique et Ingénierie des Protéines, France†loop.frontiersin.org cite67†JL Jodi L Camberg University of Rhode Island, United States†loop.frontiersin.org L244: \nL245: Outline\nL246: \nL247:   * cite68†Abstract L248:   * cite69†Introduction L249:   * cite70†Materials and Methods L250:   * cite71†Results L251:   * cite72†Discussion L252:   * cite73†Statements L253:   * cite74†References L254: \nL255: Figures and Tables\nL256: \nL257:   * Figure 1\nL258: cite75†Image cite76†View in article L259:   * Figure 2\nL260: \nL261: cite77†Image cite78†View in article L262:   * Figure 3\nL263: \nL264: cite79†Image cite80†View in article L265:   * Figure 4\nL266: \nL267: cite81†Image cite82†View in article L268:   * Figure 5\nL269: \nL270: cite83†Image cite84†View in article L271:   * Figure 6\nL272: \nL273: cite85†Image cite86†View in article L274: ## ORIGINAL RESEARCH article\nL275: \nL276: Front. Mol. Biosci., 15 April 2021\nL277: \nL278: Sec. Protein Folding, Misfolding and Degradation\nL279: \nL280: Volume 8 - 2021 | cite62†https://doi.org/10.3389/fmolb.2021.653073†doi.org L281: # Bacterial Hsp90 Facilitates the Degradation of Aggregation-Prone Hsp70–Hsp40 Substrates\nL282: \nL283:   * cite87†BF Bruno Fauvet ^{1}†loop.frontiersin.org L284:   * A F\nL285: \nL286: Andrija Finka ^{2}\nL287: \nL288:   * M C\nL289: \nL290: Marie-Pierre Castanié-Cornet ^{3}\nL291: \nL292:   * A C\nL293: \nL294: Anne-Marie Cirinesi ^{3}\nL295:   * cite88†PG Pierre Genevaux ^{3}†loop.frontiersin.org L296:   * cite89†MQ Manfredo Quadroni ^{4}†loop.frontiersin.org L297:   * cite90†PG Pierre Goloubinoff ^{1}^{*}†loop.frontiersin.org L298:   *   * 1. Department of Plant Molecular Biology (DBMV), University of Lausanne, Lausanne, Switzerland\nL299: \nL300:   * 2. Department of Ecology, Agronomy and Aquaculture, University of Zadar, Zadar, Croatia\nL301:   * 3. Laboratoire de Microbiologie et de Génétique Moléculaires, Center de Biologie Intégrative, CNRS, Université de Toulouse, Toulouse, France\nL302: \nL303:   * 4. Protein Analysis Facility, University of Lausanne, Lausanne, Switzerland\nL304: \nL305:   * [Button: See more]\nL306: \nL307: Article metrics\nL308: \nL309: cite91†View details L310: ## Abstract\nL311: In eukaryotes, the 90-kDa heat shock proteins (Hsp90s) are profusely studied chaperones that, together with 70-kDa heat shock proteins (Hsp70s), control protein homeostasis. In bacteria, however, the function of Hsp90 (HtpG) and its collaboration with Hsp70 (DnaK) remains poorly characterized.\nL312: To uncover physiological processes that depend on HtpG and DnaK, we performed comparative quantitative proteomic analyses of insoluble and total protein fractions from unstressed wild-type (WT) Escherichia coli and from knockout mutants ΔdnaKdnaJ (ΔKJ), ΔhtpG (ΔG), and ΔdnaKdnaJΔhtpG (ΔKJG). Whereas the ΔG mutant showed no detectable proteomic differences with wild-type, ΔKJ expressed more chaperones, proteases and ribosomes and expressed dramatically less metabolic and respiratory enzymes.\nL313: Unexpectedly, we found that the triple mutant ΔKJG showed higher levels of metabolic and respiratory enzymes than ΔKJ, suggesting that bacterial Hsp90 mediates the degradation of aggregation-prone Hsp70–Hsp40 substrates. Further in vivo experiments suggest that such Hsp90-mediated degradation possibly occurs through the HslUV protease.\nL314: ## Introduction\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChecking your browser - reCAPTCHA (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4316790/)\nciteturn10view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4316790/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 3\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChecking your browser - reCAPTCHA (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3158428/)\nciteturn10view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3158428/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 3\n"
